---
import { process } from "../data/evidence";
---

<section class="process-section page-width" aria-labelledby="process-heading">
  <div>
    <p class="project-kind">Agent workflows</p>
    <h2 id="process-heading">A record you<br />can follow.</h2>
    <p>
      Sprint Loops keeps the request, changes, checks, and release evidence in
      the project itself. This site's buyer guide provides a real example.
    </p>
    <a class="text-link" href={process.repository}
      >Explore Sprint Loops <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
    >
  </div>
  <ol
    class="process-record"
    aria-label="Records from this site's September 6 update"
  >
    <li>
      <span>Requested</span><p>Publish a local LLM buyer guide.</p><a
        href={process.task}>Read the task record</a
      >
    </li>
    <li>
      <span>Checked</span><p>
        Article pages, links, metadata, and the inquiry path.
      </p><a href={process.checks}>Read the recorded checks</a>
    </li>
    <li>
      <span>Published</span><p>The guide and its live deployment evidence.</p><a
        href={process.release}>Read the release record</a
      >
    </li>
  </ol>
  <p class="caption process-caption">
    Recorded September 6, 2026. This is work on my own site, not a client
    result. <a href={process.guide}>Read the guide.</a>
  </p>
</section>
